\title{caEditR: Cell-Type-Resolved RNA-Editing Deconvolution and Cell-Type Editing QTLs}
\description{
Deconvolves bulk RNA-editing-ratio matrices (sites x samples) into per-cell-type editing estimates, using each sample's cell-type proportions and each site's host-gene expression per cell type (RNA share) and read coverage: caRD_edit() (with a sorted-cell reference), caNRD_edit() (no reference; parameters estimated from the bulk cohort by maximum likelihood) and TCA_Like() (a wrapper around the CRAN 'TCA' package). Tests cell-type-specific genetic effects on editing (edQTLs) with a joint likelihood model: celltype_edqtl() and caNRD_editQTL(), including a batched scan engine for genome-wide cis scans. Builds genotype-informed cell-type editing matrices with caNRD_editQTL_shrink() and caNRD_joint_reconstruction(). Also provides cell-type proportion and expression-weight estimation, mapping of sites to host genes (hg19/hg38), coverage derived from gene expression, and simulators of cohorts with known truth. Part of the original deconvolution math runs in a bundled Python implementation called in a subprocess; the edQTL, reconstruction and simulation functions are implemented in R and C++.
